hw/sh4: ze0 speed-pulse and gyro ADC pages with the 100 ms tick (TODO M8.H32).

navdrv.dll maps 0xffc5b000 (speed-pulse capture) and 0xffc5a000 (gyro
ADC) with VirtualCopy, so the guest uses the area-7 aliases 0x1fc5b000
and 0x1fc5a000.  Its sample thread (US card ROM B fn 0x039e55b0, NK1
+0x310000) waits on SYSINTR 46, which the NK1 OAL table routes from
INTEVT 0x760 (ISR 0x8803f004, IntrPrio 11, masks INT2 bit 22).  Without
that interrupt no dead-reckoning sample reached Navi and the locator's
vehicle-speed input stayed 0.

The new ze0-dr object (/machine/dr) raises INTEVT 0x760 every tick-ms
(100) of virtual time once the driver has written the latch enable
(+0x08), drops it on the status-clear write (+0x18), returns a pulse
counter latched per tick at +0x0c and the tick count at +0x10, and the
gyro words at +0x30..+0x4c.  Inputs are QOM properties set at run time
with HMP qom-set: pulses-milli (pulses per tick x 1000), gyro0..gyro7,
tick-ms.  ZE0_DR_TRACE=1 in the environment logs the first 200 register
accesses to stderr.

Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>


